---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';

// Claim-verified against source 2026-08-10 before writing, like /privacy
// and /terms. "there won't be one" is a CONSCIOUS promise, not an
// oversight: it forecloses the deferred sign-in decision, and the
// deferred-decisions row was closed in the same commit — accounts are not
// a feature we declined, they are a thing the architecture makes
// unnecessary, and the abuse case sign-in was reserved for is handled by
// rate limiting. If abuse ever outpaces that, the promise breaks
// PUBLICLY: this page changes first, the feature comes second.
// No last-updated date: this page makes no dated promises and has no
// changes section — gitDateOf is a legal-pages mechanism.
---

<Layout
	title="About — ImageExtract"
	description="ImageExtract lists every image on a web page for preview, filtering, and download. Free, no account, nothing stored — built by an independent developer."
>
	<SiteHeader anchorPrefix="/" nav={false} />
	<main class="mx-auto max-w-content px-md py-xl">
		<article class="about-article">
			<h1 class="text-h1 font-semibold text-text">About</h1>
			<p class="mt-md text-body text-muted">
				ImageExtract lists every image on a web page so you can preview, filter, and download the
				ones you want.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-sm text-body text-muted">
				It's free, there's no account, and there won't be one.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-xl text-h3 font-semibold text-text">Why it works this way</h2>
			<p class="mt-sm text-body text-muted">
				Most tools like this open your page in a real browser on their servers, which means
				downloading every image on it whether you want them or not. That costs money on every
				scan, which is why they need signups and paid tiers.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-sm text-body text-muted">
				ImageExtract reads the page's HTML instead. It's fast, it costs almost nothing to run,
				and it means your images and the pages you scan never sit on our servers. That's not a
				policy we could change later — it's just how the thing is built.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-sm text-body text-muted">
				The tradeoff: pages that build their galleries entirely with JavaScript will return
				less. Most sites work fine.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-xl text-h3 font-semibold text-text">Who made it</h2>
			<p class="mt-sm text-body text-muted">
				An independent developer. Not a company, not funded, not collecting anything to sell.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-xl text-h3 font-semibold text-text">Contact</h2>
			<p class="mt-sm mb-xl text-body text-muted">
				<strong class="text-text">abuse@imageextract.pics</strong> for site owners and takedown
				requests. See <a href="/traffic" class="text-accent hover:underline">Traffic</a> for what
				our requests to your site actually do.
			</p>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	/* Reading measure: half the content width, derived from the container
	   token rather than an invented value (the .hero-form precedent). */
	.about-article {
		max-width: calc(var(--container-content) / 2);
	}
</style>
